b.com/users/emilyfertig/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilyfertig","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\n\nIt seems colocated_python is intended to work on TPU hosts without Pathways, but it doesn't seem very tested. Here's a failure from doing something straightforward on a v6e-8 host (have also seen it on a v5p-8 host):\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport jax\nfrom jax.experimental import colocated_python\nimport numpy as np\n\nos.environ['XLA_FLAGS'] = '--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=8'\n\nsharding = jax.NamedSharding(\n    jax.sharding.Mesh(jax.devices(), ['i']), jax.sharding.PartitionSpec('i')\n)\ncpu_sharding = jax.NamedSharding(\n    colocated_python.colocated_cpu_devices(sharding.mesh), sharding.spec\n)\n\njax.device_put(\n    jax.device_put(np.zeros(16), sharding), cpu_sharding\n).addressable_shards[0].index\n```\nThis produces `KeyError: CpuDevice(id=0)`.\n\n(Though actually I can see this is only related to colocated_python insofar as its colocated_cpu_devices requires multiple CPU devices on host, and the same error happens with jax.devices('cpu') without actually using `colocated_cpu_devices`.)\n\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\njax:    0.8.1\njaxlib: 0.8.1\nnumpy:  2.3.4\npython: 3.12.11 (stable, redacted, redacted) [Clang 9999.0.0 (704240125ddf17b9b4995871af3759c742a202ba)]\ndevice info: TPU v6 lite-8, 8 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Linux', release='5.10.0-smp-1105.52.646.6', version='#1 [v5.10.0-1105.52.646.6] SMP @1755285215', machine='x86_64')\nXLA_FLAGS=--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=8","closed_at":"2025-11-18T01:40:53Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/44061?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/copybara-service%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"